    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192749": {
      "title": "Kraft Family Professor of Jewish Studies",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Kraft Family Professor of Jewish Studies Rice University: School of Humanities and Arts Location Houston, Texas Open Date Sep 02, 2026 Description The Center for Jewish Studies in the School of Humanities and Arts at Rice University is seeking to hire the Kraft Family Professor of Jewish Studies, a full-time senior level scholar in modern Jewish Studies who will also serve as the next Center Director for a renewable term of 3–5 years. As the next Center Director, we are seeking an individual who has significant administrative and institution-building experience, is strategic, inspirational, and visionary, with a broad-minded and interdisciplinary approach to Jewish Studies. The successful candidate must qualify for an appointment in one of the departments in the School of Humanities and Arts. We are seeking a candidate with broad experience and familiarity with many levels and avenues of public engagement with Jewish culture and history, theoretical positions, and cutting-edge research; an experimental mindset; and the desire to foster a collaborative research environment in a diverse educational setting. The center’s curriculum and research clusters are in dialogue with other departments, centers, and programs across the humanities (such as History; Religion; Modern and Classical Languages, Literatures, and Cultures; English and Creative Writing; Art History; and Media Studies). These research clusters also aim to connect with interdisciplinary centers like the Boniuk Institute for the Study and Advancement of Religious Tolerance, the Center for the Study of Women, Gender, and Sexuality and the Center for Latin American and Latinx Studies. We seek a candidate who can participate in the process of expanding and redefining a Jewish Studies curriculum and building research initiatives in this dynamic context. The Center for Jewish Studies—which formally elevated from a program to a center on July 1, 2026—aims to convene an active community of faculty and postdoctoral scholars whose collaborations elevate Rice’s profile internationally. A successful candidate will bring organizational and strategic thought leadership as future Center Director; shape the academic profile of the newly created Center; engage and maintain an active and ambitious program of research and scholarship; foster innovative research clusters; collaborate with the curator of the Joan and Stanford Alexander South Texas Jewish Archives; participate in student mentoring and advising; teach and develop courses, and serve on department and university committees. The search is particularly interested in candidates whose scholarly focus is in the 19th and 20th  centuries and in one of the following fields: Jewish thought, history, or culture; Holocaust Studies; or the critical study of modern antisemitism. Candidates must hold a PhD in Jewish Studies, History, Religion, Cultural Studies, Literary Studies, English, Art History, or a closely related field in the humanities.  Required qualifications include a proven record of distinguished scholarly publication commensurate with appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, administrative and leadership experience at the department or center/program level, exceptional organizational and collaborative skills, and a strong record of undergraduate- or graduate-level teaching and mentoring. Review of applications will begin immediately, continuing until the position is filled. For fullest consideration, application materials should be submitted by November 10, 2026. All applications must be submitted via Interfolio [https://apply.interfolio.com/192749].  Appointment begins July 1, 2027. Applicants should upload: A cover letter summarizing your interest and qualifications for both the endowed chair and the Center directorship. A current curriculum vitae, including a summary of your administrative and institution-building experience. A statement of research outlining your ongoing agenda, publication plan, and vision for interdisciplinary research clusters. A statement of teaching philosophy, including courses you could offer at the undergraduate level. Representative publications appropriate to your discipline (scholarly articles or book excerpts). Contact information for 3 to 5 professional references. Rice University is a highly selective and highly ranked private research university with approximately 4,800 undergraduate and 4,100 graduate students, supported by 900 full- and part-time faculty. Rice University is committed to groundbreaking research and unsurpassed education for the betterment of the world. It is known for its commitment to equitable access for students of all economic backgrounds and to freedom of scholarly inquiry. Rice is located in Houston, Texas, a culturally diverse metropolitan city with a vibrant intellectual, museum, and cultural community. The Center for Jewish Studies enjoys strong cross-disciplinary partnerships across the university and collaborates with regional partners such as Holocaust Museum Houston and the Texas Medical Center. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Rice University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with commitment to diversity at all levels, and considers for employment qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, genetic information, disability or protected veteran status. Rice Mission and Values : Mission and Values | Rice University © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
