    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195430": {
      "title": "Faculty Position in Astronomy, Astro-Particle Physics and Cosmology",
      "description": "Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Faculty Position in Astronomy, Astro-Particle Physics and Cosmology Rice University: Wiess School of Natural Sciences: Physics and Astronomy Location Houston, Texas Open Date Oct 09, 2026 Deadline Dec 10, 2026 at 11:59 PM Eastern Time Description Faculty Position in Astronomy, Astro-Particle Physics and Cosmology Rice University The Department of Physics and Astronomy at Rice University in Houston, Texas, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position as part of an AI Initiative hire. Candidates must demonstrate expertise in at least one key emerging area, such as generative AI, agentic systems, or physical AI, extending beyond traditional machine learning tools. They should possess the ability to develop advanced computational frameworks, physics-informed AI methodologies, or innovative algorithmic tools, and integrate them into theory, simulation, data analysis, or instrumentation pipelines. Successful candidates will focus their research program on one or a subset of the following areas: star-planet interactions, exoplanetary science, astro-particle physics, or cosmology. Depending on the exact expertise of the final hire, the hire will be required to measurably strengthen connections between the Nuclear and Particle Physics group and the Relativistic Astrophysics and Cosmology group, or between the Space Plasma Physics and Astrophysics of Star and Planet formation groups. Ultimately, this hire will foster interdisciplinary collaboration, establish a shared AI ecosystem across domains, and build connections with the Ken Kennedy Institute, the Rice Space Institute, and the T.W. Bonner Laboratory. We seek outstanding scientists whose research will complement and extend existing activities within the Department and across the University. In addition to developing an independent and vigorous research program, the successful applicant will be expected to teach, on average, one undergraduate or graduate course each semester, playing a critical role in integrating modern AI concepts systematically throughout our curricula to train the next generation of scientists fluent in AI-enabled discovery, and contribute to the service missions of the Department and University. The Department anticipates making an appointment at the assistant professor level. A Ph.D. in physics, astronomy, or a related field is required by the time of appointment. Applications for this position must be submitted electronically at https://apply.interfolio.com/195430 . We will begin reviewing applications by December 1, 2026. To receive full consideration, all application materials must be received by December 10, 2026. The anticipated start date is July 1, 2027. Applicants are required to submit the following: (1) cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) statement of research; (4) statement on teaching; and (5) PDF copies (or links) of three publications considered to be the most important. Additionally, applicants must arrange for three letters of reference to be submitted via Interfolio by December 10, 2026. For additional information, please contact the search chairs, Dr. Paul Padley (padley@rice.edu) and Dr. Andrea Isella (isella@rice.edu). Qualified applicants are considered without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. Also, in our candidate pools, we seek to attract greater representation of women, scholars of color, people with disabilities, veterans, and others who have historically been underrepresented in Physics. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Rice University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with commitment to diversity at all levels, and considers for employment qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, genetic information, disability or protected veteran status. Rice Mission and Values : Mission and Values | Rice University © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling