    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195709": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Positions in Artificial Intelligence for Sustainability and Resilience",
      "description": "Posted: Oct 15, 2026 Apply - Interfolio undefined page loaded Skip to Main Content Already have an account? Sign In Assistant Professor Positions in Artificial Intelligence for Sustainability and Resilience Rice University: Brown School of Engineering and Computing Location Houston, TX Open Date Oct 15, 2026 Description Assistant Professor Positions in Artificial Intelligence for Sustainability and Resilience Two Tenure-Track Faculty Openings in the George R. Brown School of Engineering and Computing at Rice University https://engineering.rice.edu/ https://www.rice.edu/ Position Description The George R. Brown School of Engineering and Computing at Rice University in Houston, Texas, invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in artificial intelligence for sustainability and resilience, with anticipated start dates of July 1, 2027. These positions are part of a coordinated, school-wide initiative to build strength in technically rigorous AI and its application to consequential scientific and engineering challenges. We seek candidates who develop, advance, or apply artificial intelligence to address challenges in sustainability and resilience. We welcome research across a broad range of scientific and engineering domains that combines technical depth in AI with the potential for significant impact on sustainable and resilient systems. Successful candidates will demonstrate technical depth in AI scholarship and clear potential for transformative domain impact. Rice seeks faculty who embrace a culture of excellence, innovation, collaboration, responsible technological development, and inclusive mentorship. Excellence in research and teaching will be the primary criteria for evaluation. Responsibilities The selected candidate will be expected to establish or maintain a vigorous, externally funded research program with national and international recognition; conduct innovative research and disseminate results through high-impact publications, conferences, and other scholarly activities; and teach undergraduate and graduate courses aligned with their expertise. Additional responsibilities include advising and mentoring undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral researchers; contributing to departmental, school, university, and professional service; and fostering interdisciplinary collaborations within Rice and with external partners. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, advising, and mentoring students from a broad range of backgrounds and experiences and will contribute to the continued strength of undergraduate and graduate education across the department and the George R. Brown School of Engineering and Computing. Rice’s highly collaborative environment provides opportunities to engage with researchers in materials science, computational science, energy, advanced manufacturing, biomedical engineering, and other disciplines. We welcome the fullness of diversity at Rice. Qualified applicants are considered without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, genetic information, disability, or protected veteran status. In our candidate pools, we seek to increase the representation of women, scholars of color, people with disabilities, veterans, and others who have historically been underrepresented in engineering, computing, and the statistical sciences; attract scholars and students from a wide range of countries, backgrounds, and experiences; accelerate progress toward building a faculty and staff community with diverse perspectives and expertise; and maintain an environment that fosters interaction, understanding, and belonging throughout our community. About the School of Engineering and Computing’s AI Initiative The School’s Vision 2030 strategic plan identifies three research thrusts: Health and Well-being, Sustainability and Resilience, and Computing and AI. Consistent with that broader vision, Rice Engineering and Computing is undertaking a multi-year faculty hiring initiative in artificial intelligence. For the 2026–27 hiring cycle, the School is recruiting for three positions: one open-rank position in Foundational AI and two Assistant Professor positions in AI for Sustainability and Resilience. The initiative prioritizes deep, technically rigorous AI scholarship, interdisciplinary collaboration, responsible technological development, and research with the potential for significant scientific and societal impact. Within this initiative, the two AI for Sustainability and Resilience positions lie at the intersection of the Computing and AI and Sustainability and Resilience thrusts. This search prioritizes domain-specific applications of AI to engineering, materials, environmental systems, and sustainability. It supports the School’s goals of reinventing what we make; transforming how and where we live; and designing technologies and infrastructure that anticipate and respond to environmental, societal, and space-related challenges. Candidates applying through this posting will be considered for a potential primary appointment in Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Civil and Environmental Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Statistics, Computer Science, or Electrical and Computer Engineering. Candidates whose work aligns with multiple departments may be reviewed across multiple applicant pools, and joint or affiliated appointments may also be considered. About Rice University Rice University is a private, comprehensive research university located on a 300-acre, tree-lined campus in Houston, Texas, adjacent to the Texas Medical Center. Rice serves nearly 9,200 undergraduate and graduate students and is distinguished by research excellence, a collaborative culture, and close engagement between students and faculty. Houston’s leadership in energy, health care, aerospace, manufacturing, and data-intensive industries creates exceptional opportunities for external partnerships and research impact. Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in chemical or biomolecular engineering; civil or environmental engineering; mechanical or aerospace engineering; statistics, or data science; computer science or machine learning; electrical or computer engineering; applied mathematics; operations research; materials science; environmental science; or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate excellence or exceptional promise in research and scholarship; the potential to establish a highly impactful, externally funded research program; a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching; and a commitment to mentoring students and contributing to a collaborative academic community. Application Instructions For full consideration, applications should be received by December 1, 2026. Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. Applicants must submit the following materials through Interfolio: 1. Curriculum vitae 2. Research statement, up to five pages 3. Statement of teaching philosophy, up to two pages 4. Names and contact information for three to five professional references. Letters of reference will be requested only if the candidate advances to the interview stage. Applicants will also be asked in Interfolio to indicate their first and second preferred home departments from the following eligible options: Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Civil and Environmental Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Statistics, Computer Science, and Electrical and Computer Engineering. Application Process This institution is using Interfolio's Faculty Search to conduct\n            this search. Applicants to this position receive a free Dossier\n            account and can send all application materials, including\n            confidential letters of recommendation, free of charge. Apply Now Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Rice University is an Equal Opportunity Employer with commitment to diversity at all levels, and considers for employment qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national or ethnic origin, genetic information, disability or protected veteran status. Rice Mission and Values : Mission and Values | Rice University © 2026 Elsevier Inc. or its licensors and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. Support | Careers | Accessibility Policy | Cookies Settings | Privacy Policy | Terms of Service We use cookies that are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyze, improve, and personalize our content and your digital experience. You can manage your cookie preferences using the Cookie settings link. For more information, see our Cookie Policy Cookie settings Accept all cookies Opt-Out Request Honored Cookie Preference Center We use cookies which are necessary to make our site work. We may also use additional cookies to analyse, improve and personalise our content and your digital experience. For more information, see our Cookie Policy and the list of Google Ad-Tech Vendors . You may choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types may impact your experience of our site and the services we are able to offer. See the different category headings below to find out more or change your settings. You may also be able to exercise your privacy choices as described in our Privacy Policy Allow all Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Always active These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Cookie Details List‎ Functional Cookies Functional Cookies These cookies enable the website to provide enhanced functionality and personalisation. They may be set by us or by third party providers whose services we have added to our pages. If you do not allow these cookies then some or all of these services may not function properly. Cookie Details List‎ Performance Cookies Performance Cookies These cookies allow us to count visits and traffic sources so we can measure and improve the performance of our site. They help us to know which pages are the most and least popular and see how visitors move around the site. Cookie Details List‎ Targeting Cookies Targeting Cookies These cookies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. If you do not allow these cookies, you will experience less targeted advertising. Cookie Details List‎ Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Confirm my choices"
